IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssc-core`
IMPORT `ssc1-prelim`
IMPORT `ssc1-class1`

-- Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 (United Kingdom), 1992 c. 4.
-- Part I, Class 1A contributions (ss 10 to 10ZC) and Class 1B contributions (s 10A): src lines 356-473.
-- Part agent ssc1, LAYER 1. Source: a plain-text rendering by a converter script, not the official text.
--
-- Reading a result: JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE is the text answering in its own words; NOTHING is "not covered".
-- The Class 1A and Class 1B percentage is "a percentage rate equal to the secondary percentage for the tax year in question"
-- (s 10(5), s 10A(6)); the secondary percentage is s 9(2) (ssc1-class1.l4), so the amount functions take it as an input.
-- The income-tax terms (general earnings, benefits code, PAYE settlement agreement, non-cash voucher, sporting testimonial payment)
-- are the Income Tax (Earnings and Pensions) Act 2003's and are asked as facts.

§ `Part I -- Class 1A and Class 1B contributions, ss 10 to 10A`

§§ `s 10 Class 1A contributions`

-- s 10(1): where an earner is chargeable to income tax on general earnings from an employment that is employed earner's employment and
-- a benefits-code employment (not lower-paid employment as a minister of religion), and the general earnings, or part, are left out
-- of the Class 1 computation, a Class 1A contribution is payable for the tax year in respect of the earner and the part left out.
-- src:358 | (1) Where—
-- src:359 | (a) for any tax year an earner is chargeable to income tax under ITEPA 2003 on an amount of general earnings received by him from any employment (“the relevant employment”),
-- src:360 | (b) the relevant employment is both—
-- src:361 | (i) employed earner’s employment, and
-- src:362 | (ii) an employment, other than lower-paid employment as a minister of religion, within the meaning of the benefits code (see Chapter 2 of Part 3 of ITEPA 2003), and
-- src:363 | (c) the whole or a part of the general earnings falls, for the purposes of Class 1 contributions, to be left out of account in the computation of the earnings paid to or for the benefit of the earner,
-- src:364 | a Class 1A contribution shall be payable for that tax year, in accordance with this section, in respect of that earner and so much of the general earnings as falls to be so left out of account.
@ref s 10(1) (src:358-364)
GIVEN `the earner is chargeable to income tax under ITEPA 2003 on general earnings received from the employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employment is employed earner's employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employment is an employment, other than lower-paid employment as a minister of religion, within the meaning of the benefits code` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the whole or a part of the general earnings falls, for the purposes of Class 1 contributions, to be left out of account` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10(1) a Class 1A contribution is payable for the tax year` MEANS
    IF     `the earner is chargeable to income tax under ITEPA 2003 on general earnings received from the employment`
       AND `the employment is employed earner's employment`
       AND `the employment is an employment, other than lower-paid employment as a minister of religion, within the meaning of the benefits code`
       AND `the whole or a part of the general earnings falls, for the purposes of Class 1 contributions, to be left out of account`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where" all four conditions hold a Class 1A contribution "shall be payable"; the subsection is silent outside them

-- s 10(1A) to (1C): the contribution on a termination award.
-- src:365 | (1A) A Class 1A contribution is payable for a tax year, in accordance with this section, in respect of an earner and the amount of a termination award if and so far as—
-- src:366 | (a) that amount counts as employment income of the earner under section 403 of ITEPA 2003 (charge on termination payments or benefits), and
-- src:367 | (b) the earner is chargeable to income tax on that amount for the tax year by virtue of that section.
@ref s 10(1A) (src:365-367)
GIVEN `the amount counts as employment income of the earner under section 403 of ITEPA 2003` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the earner is chargeable to income tax on that amount for the tax year by virtue of that section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10(1A) a Class 1A contribution is payable for the tax year in respect of the termination award` MEANS
    IF     `the amount counts as employment income of the earner under section 403 of ITEPA 2003`
       AND `the earner is chargeable to income tax on that amount for the tax year by virtue of that section`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A Class 1A contribution is payable for a tax year ... if and so far as (a) that amount counts as employment income ... and (b) the earner is chargeable to income tax on that amount" (marginal reading M1(a))

-- src:368 | (1B) No Class 1A contribution is payable under subsection (1A) in respect of an amount so far as it is an amount of earnings in respect of which Class 1 contributions are payable.
@ref s 10(1B) (src:368-368)
GIVEN `the amount is an amount of earnings in respect of which Class 1 contributions are payable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10(1B) a Class 1A contribution is payable under subsection (1A) in respect of the amount` MEANS
    IF `the amount is an amount of earnings in respect of which Class 1 contributions are payable`
    THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No Class 1A contribution is payable under subsection (1A) in respect of an amount so far as it is an amount of earnings in respect of which Class 1 contributions are payable"
    ELSE NOTHING       -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is for the amount "so far as" it is Class 1 earnings

-- src:369 | (1C) No Class 1A contribution is payable under subsection (1A) unless the employment which is terminated is employed earner's employment.
@ref s 10(1C) (src:369-369)
GIVEN `the employment which is terminated is employed earner's employment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10(1C) a Class 1A contribution is payable under subsection (1A)` MEANS
    IF `the employment which is terminated is employed earner's employment`
    THEN NOTHING       -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "unless" states a necessary condition only
    ELSE JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No Class 1A contribution is payable under subsection (1A) unless the employment which is terminated is employed earner's employment"

-- s 10(2) and (3A): who pays. Subject to sections 10ZA and 10ZBA, the person liable for the secondary Class 1 contribution on the
-- last (or only) relevant payment of earnings in the tax year; if there is none, the person who would be liable if the general
-- earnings were earnings. Sections 10ZA(3) and 10ZBA(2) move the liability: their answers are the inputs.
DECLARE `s 10(2) Who pays the Class 1A contribution` IS ONE OF
    `s 10(2)(a) the person liable to pay the secondary Class 1 contribution relating to the last (or only) relevant payment of earnings in the tax year`
    `s 10(2)(b) the person who would be liable to pay the secondary Class 1 contribution if the general earnings were earnings in respect of which Class 1 contributions would be payable`
    `s 10ZA(3) the person providing the benefit`
    `s 10ZBA(2) the controller of the sporting testimonial`

-- src:370 | (2) Subject to sections 10ZA and 10ZBA, a Class 1A contribution payable under subsection (1) for any tax year shall be payable by—
-- src:371 | (a) the person who is liable to pay the secondary Class 1 contribution relating to the last (or only) relevant payment of earnings in that tax year in relation to which there is a liability to pay such a Class 1 contribution; or
-- src:372 | (b) if paragraph (a) above does not apply, the person who, if the general earnings in respect of which the Class 1A contribution is payable were earnings in respect of which Class 1 contributions would be payable, would be liable to pay the secondary Class 1 contribution.
@ref s 10(2) (src:370-372)
GIVEN `there is a last (or only) relevant payment of earnings in the tax year in relation to which there is a liability to pay a secondary Class 1 contribution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 10ZA(3) the liability falls on the person providing the benefit` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 10ZBA(2) the liability falls on the controller of the sporting testimonial` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 10(2) Who pays the Class 1A contribution`
`s 10(2) who pays the Class 1A contribution payable under subsection (1)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 10ZBA(2) the liability falls on the controller of the sporting testimonial` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST `s 10ZBA(2) the controller of the sporting testimonial`
        IF `s 10ZA(3) the liability falls on the person providing the benefit` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST `s 10ZA(3) the person providing the benefit`
        IF `s 10ZBA(2) the liability falls on the controller of the sporting testimonial` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether section 10ZBA moves the liability was not answered
        IF `s 10ZA(3) the liability falls on the person providing the benefit` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether section 10ZA moves the liability was not answered
        IF `there is a last (or only) relevant payment of earnings in the tax year in relation to which there is a liability to pay a secondary Class 1 contribution` THEN JUST `s 10(2)(a) the person liable to pay the secondary Class 1 contribution relating to the last (or only) relevant payment of earnings in the tax year`
        OTHERWISE JUST `s 10(2)(b) the person who would be liable to pay the secondary Class 1 contribution if the general earnings were earnings in respect of which Class 1 contributions would be payable`

-- src:373 | (3) In subsection (2) above “relevant payment of earnings” means a payment which for the purposes of Class 1 contributions is a payment of earnings made to or for the benefit of the earner in respect of the relevant employment.
@ref s 10(3) (src:373-373)
GIVEN `the payment is, for the purposes of Class 1 contributions, a payment of earnings made to or for the benefit of the earner in respect of the relevant employment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10(3) the payment is a relevant payment of earnings` MEANS
    IF `the payment is, for the purposes of Class 1 contributions, a payment of earnings made to or for the benefit of the earner in respect of the relevant employment`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“relevant payment of earnings” means a payment which for the purposes of Class 1 contributions is a payment of earnings made to or for the benefit of the earner in respect of the relevant employment"

-- src:374 | (3A) A Class 1A contribution payable under subsection (1A) is payable by the person who, if the amount in respect of which the Class 1A contribution is payable were earnings in respect of which Class 1 contributions would be payable, would be liable to pay the secondary Class 1 contribution.
@ref s 10(3A) (src:374-374)
GIVEN `s 10(1A) a Class 1A contribution is payable under subsection (1A)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 10(2) Who pays the Class 1A contribution`
`s 10(3A) who pays the Class 1A contribution payable under subsection (1A)` MEANS
    IF `s 10(1A) a Class 1A contribution is payable under subsection (1A)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST `s 10(2)(b) the person who would be liable to pay the secondary Class 1 contribution if the general earnings were earnings in respect of which Class 1 contributions would be payable`
    ELSE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A Class 1A contribution payable under subsection (1A) is payable by the person who ..."

-- s 10(4), (4A), (5): the amount is the Class 1A percentage of the part left out (4) or of the termination award (4A); the Class 1A
-- percentage equals the secondary percentage for the tax year in question (5).
-- src:377 | (5) In subsections (4) and (4A) above “the Class 1A percentage” means a percentage rate equal to the secondary percentage for the tax year in question.
@ref s 10(5) (src:377-377)
GIVEN `s 9(2) the secondary percentage for the tax year in question` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 10(5) the Class 1A percentage` MEANS `s 9(2) the secondary percentage for the tax year in question`

-- src:375 | (4) The amount of the Class 1A contribution payable under subsection (1) in respect of any general earnings shall be the Class 1A percentage of so much of them as falls to be left out of account as mentioned in subsection (1)(c) above.
@ref s 10(4) (src:375-375)
GIVEN `s 10(1) a Class 1A contribution is payable` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the general earnings that fall to be left out of account` IS A NUMBER
      `s 10(5) the Class 1A percentage` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 10(4) the amount of the Class 1A contribution payable under subsection (1)` MEANS
    IF `s 10(1) a Class 1A contribution is payable` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (`s 10(5) the Class 1A percentage` TIMES `the general earnings that fall to be left out of account`)
    ELSE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the amount is that of a contribution "payable under subsection (1)"

-- src:376 | (4A) The amount of the Class 1A contribution payable under subsection (1A) in respect of an amount is the Class 1A percentage of that amount.
@ref s 10(4A) (src:376-376)
GIVEN `s 10(1A) a Class 1A contribution is payable under subsection (1A)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the amount of the termination award` IS A NUMBER
      `s 10(5) the Class 1A percentage` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 10(4A) the amount of the Class 1A contribution payable under subsection (1A)` MEANS
    IF `s 10(1A) a Class 1A contribution is payable under subsection (1A)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (`s 10(5) the Class 1A percentage` TIMES `the amount of the termination award`)
    ELSE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the amount is that of a contribution "payable under subsection (1A)"

-- s 10(6): no Class 1A contribution is payable for the year on general earnings taken, for Class 1B, to be included in a PAYE settlement agreement.
-- src:378 | (6) No Class 1A contribution shall be payable for any tax year in respect of so much of any general earnings as are taken for the purposes of the making of Class 1B contributions for that year to be included in a PAYE settlement agreement.
@ref s 10(6) (src:378-378)
GIVEN `the general earnings are taken for the purposes of the making of Class 1B contributions for the year to be included in a PAYE settlement agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10(6) a Class 1A contribution is payable in respect of the general earnings` MEANS
    IF `the general earnings are taken for the purposes of the making of Class 1B contributions for the year to be included in a PAYE settlement agreement`
    THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No Class 1A contribution shall be payable for any tax year in respect of so much of any general earnings as are taken ... to be included in a PAYE settlement agreement"
    ELSE NOTHING       -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is for general earnings taken to be included in a PAYE settlement agreement

-- s 10(7), (7A), (7B): in working out the general earnings received, a deduction under an excluded provision is disregarded; but where
-- the deduction allowed is at least the whole of the corresponding amount that would be included, that whole amount is treated as not included.
DECLARE `s 10(7B) Provision of ITEPA 2003` IS ONE OF
    `s 10(7B)(a) a provision of Chapter 2 of Part 5 other than section 352`
    `s 10(7B)(a) section 352 (limited deduction for agency fees paid by entertainers)`
    `s 10(7B)(aa) any of sections 363 to 365`
    `s 10(7B)(b) any provision of Chapter 5 of Part 5`
    `s 10(7B) another provision`

-- src:385 | (7B) For the purposes of subsections (7) and (7A) “excluded provision” means—
-- src:386 | (a) any provision of Chapter 2 of Part 5 of ITEPA 2003 (deductions for employee’s expenses), other than section 352 (limited deduction for agency fees paid by entertainers), ...
-- src:387 | (aa) any of sections 363 to 365 of ITEPA 2003 (certain deductions from benefits code earnings), or
-- src:388 | (b) any provision of Chapter 5 of Part 5 of ITEPA 2003 (deductions for earnings representing benefits or reimbursed expenses).
@ref s 10(7B) (src:385-388)
GIVEN provision IS A `s 10(7B) Provision of ITEPA 2003`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10(7B) the provision is an excluded provision` MEANS
    CONSIDER provision
    WHEN `s 10(7B)(a) a provision of Chapter 2 of Part 5 other than section 352` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 10(7B)(a) section 352 (limited deduction for agency fees paid by entertainers)` THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any provision of Chapter 2 of Part 5 of ITEPA 2003 (deductions for employee’s expenses), other than section 352"
    WHEN `s 10(7B)(aa) any of sections 363 to 365` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 10(7B)(b) any provision of Chapter 5 of Part 5` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 10(7B) another provision` THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“excluded provision” means" the listed provisions (marginal reading: the text of (7B)(a) ends with an omission, src:386)

-- src:379 | (7) In calculating for the purposes of this section the amount of general earnings received by an earner from an employment, a deduction under any of the excluded provisions is to be disregarded.
-- src:380 | This subsection does not apply in relation to a deduction if subsection (7A) applies in relation to it.
-- src:381 | (7A) Where—
-- src:382 | (a) a deduction in respect of a matter is allowed under an excluded provision, and
-- src:383 | (b) the amount deductible is at least equal to the whole of any corresponding amount which would (but for this section) fall by reference to that matter to be included in the general earnings mentioned in subsection (7),
-- src:384 | the whole of the corresponding amount shall be treated as not included.
@ref s 10(7), s 10(7A) (src:379-384)
GIVEN `the general earnings received before the deduction` IS A NUMBER
      `the deduction in respect of the matter is allowed under an excluded provision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount deductible` IS A NUMBER
      `the corresponding amount that would otherwise fall to be included in the general earnings` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 10(7) the amount of the general earnings received` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the deduction in respect of the matter is allowed under an excluded provision` THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsections (7) and (7A) speak of a deduction "under any of the excluded provisions"
        IF `the amount deductible` AT LEAST `the corresponding amount that would otherwise fall to be included in the general earnings` THEN JUST (`the general earnings received before the deduction` MINUS `the corresponding amount that would otherwise fall to be included in the general earnings`)    -- (7A): "the whole of the corresponding amount shall be treated as not included"
        OTHERWISE JUST `the general earnings received before the deduction`    -- (7): "a deduction under any of the excluded provisions is to be disregarded"

-- src:397 | (12) In this section “termination award” means a payment or benefit received by an earner (or an earner's spouse, civil partner, blood relative or dependant) in connection with the termination of the earner's employment.
@ref s 10(12) (src:397-397)
GIVEN `the payment or benefit is received by the earner, or by the earner's spouse, civil partner, blood relative or dependant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is received in connection with the termination of the earner's employment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10(12) the payment or benefit is a termination award` MEANS
    IF     `the payment or benefit is received by the earner, or by the earner's spouse, civil partner, blood relative or dependant`
       AND `it is received in connection with the termination of the earner's employment`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“termination award” means a payment or benefit received by an earner (or an earner's spouse, civil partner, blood relative or dependant) in connection with the termination of the earner's employment"

§§ `s 10ZA Liability of third party provider of benefits in kind`

-- s 10ZA(1) and (1A): the four conditions; the section does not apply to a sporting testimonial payment.
-- src:399 | (1) This section applies, where—
-- src:400 | (a) a Class 1A contribution is payable for any tax year in respect of the whole or any part of general earnings received by an earner;
-- src:401 | (b) the general earnings, in so far as they are ones in respect of which such a contribution is payable, consist in a benefit provided for the earner or a member of his family or household;
-- src:402 | (c) the person providing the benefit is a person other than the person (“the relevant employer”) by whom, but for this section, the Class 1A contribution would be payable in accordance with section 10(2) above; and
-- src:403 | (d) the provision of the benefit by that other person has not been arranged or facilitated by the relevant employer.
-- src:404 | (1A) This section does not apply if the benefit is a sporting testimonial payment (see section 10ZBA).
@ref s 10ZA(1), s 10ZA(1A) (src:399-404)
GIVEN `a Class 1A contribution is payable for the tax year in respect of the whole or any part of general earnings received by the earner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the general earnings, so far as the contribution is payable on them, consist in a benefit provided for the earner or a member of his family or household` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person providing the benefit is a person other than the relevant employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision of the benefit by that other person has not been arranged or facilitated by the relevant employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the benefit is a sporting testimonial payment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10ZA(1) section 10ZA applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the benefit is a sporting testimonial payment` THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(1A) This section does not apply if the benefit is a sporting testimonial payment"
        IF     `a Class 1A contribution is payable for the tax year in respect of the whole or any part of general earnings received by the earner`
           AND `the general earnings, so far as the contribution is payable on them, consist in a benefit provided for the earner or a member of his family or household`
           AND `the person providing the benefit is a person other than the relevant employer`
           AND `the provision of the benefit by that other person has not been arranged or facilitated by the relevant employer` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies, where" all four conditions hold

-- s 10ZA(2): a payment by the provider to discharge the earner's income tax on the benefit, or on the payment itself, is treated as a further benefit.
-- src:405 | (2) For the purposes of this Act if—
-- src:406 | (a) the person providing the benefit pays an amount for the purpose of discharging any liability of the earner to income tax for any tax year, and
-- src:407 | (b) the income tax in question is tax chargeable in respect of the provision of the benefit or of the making of the payment itself,
-- src:408 | the amount of the payment shall be treated as if it were general earnings consisting in the provision of a benefit to the earner in that tax year and falling, for the purposes of Class 1 contributions, to be left out of account in the computation of the earnings paid to or for the benefit of the earner.
@ref s 10ZA(2) (src:405-408)
GIVEN `s 10ZA(1) section 10ZA applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person providing the benefit pays an amount for the purpose of discharging any liability of the earner to income tax for any tax year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the income tax is chargeable in respect of the provision of the benefit or of the making of the payment itself` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10ZA(2) the amount of the payment is treated as general earnings consisting in the provision of a benefit to the earner in that tax year` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`s 10ZA(1) section 10ZA applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (2) is in section 10ZA, which "applies, where" the four conditions of subsection (1) hold
        IF `the person providing the benefit pays an amount for the purpose of discharging any liability of the earner to income tax for any tax year` AND `the income tax is chargeable in respect of the provision of the benefit or of the making of the payment itself` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "For the purposes of this Act if (a) ... and (b) ..., the amount of the payment shall be treated as if it were general earnings" (marginal reading M1(a))

-- s 10ZA(4): for the tax year beginning with 6 April 2000, subsection (3) applies only if the provider gave written notice to the
-- Inland Revenue on or before 6 July 2001. NOTHING for the date means no notice was given.
-- src:413 | (4) Subsection (3) above applies in the case of a Class 1A contribution for the tax year beginning with 6th April 2000 only if the person providing the benefit in question gives notice in writing to the Inland Revenue on or before 6th July 2001 that he is a person who provides benefits in respect of which a liability to Class 1A contributions is capable of falling by virtue of this section on a person other than the relevant employer.
@ref s 10ZA(4) (src:413-413)
GIVEN year IS A `Tax year`
      `the date on which the person providing the benefit gave written notice to the Inland Revenue` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10ZA(4) subsection (3) applies in the case of a Class 1A contribution for the tax year` MEANS
    IF year EQUALS `Tax year` OF 2000
    THEN
        CONSIDER `the date on which the person providing the benefit gave written notice to the Inland Revenue`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "only if the person providing the benefit in question gives notice in writing" (no notice given)
        WHEN JUST d THEN
            IF d AT MOST (Date 6 7 2001)
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "only if ... on or before 6th July 2001"
    ELSE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (4) speaks of "the tax year beginning with 6th April 2000" only

-- s 10ZA(3): the liability falls on the person providing the benefit instead of on the relevant employer.
-- src:409 | (3) Subject to subsection (4) below, the liability to pay any Class 1A contribution in respect of—
-- src:410 | (a) the benefit provided to the earner, and
-- src:411 | (b) any further benefit treated as so provided in accordance with subsection (2) above,
-- src:412 | shall fall on the person providing the benefit, instead of on the relevant employer.
@ref s 10ZA(3) (src:409-412)
GIVEN `s 10ZA(1) section 10ZA applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 10ZA(4) subsection (3) applies in the case of a Class 1A contribution for the tax year` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10ZA(3) the liability falls on the person providing the benefit` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`s 10ZA(1) section 10ZA applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (3) is within "This section applies, where" the conditions hold
        IF `s 10ZA(4) subsection (3) applies in the case of a Class 1A contribution for the tax year` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (3) above applies in the case of a Class 1A contribution for the tax year beginning with 6th April 2000 only if ..."
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:415 | (6) In this section references to a member of a person’s family or household shall be construed in accordance with section 721(5) of ITEPA 2003.
@ref s 10ZA(6) (src:415-415)
GIVEN `the person is a member of the other person's family or household within the meaning of section 721(5) of ITEPA 2003` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10ZA(6) the person is a member of a person's family or household` MEANS
    IF `the person is a member of the other person's family or household within the meaning of section 721(5) of ITEPA 2003`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "references to a member of a person’s family or household shall be construed in accordance with section 721(5) of ITEPA 2003"

§§ `s 10ZB Non-cash vouchers provided by third parties`

-- src:417 | (1) In section 10ZA above references to the provision of a benefit include references to the provision of a non-cash voucher.
@ref s 10ZB(1) (src:417-417)
GIVEN `it is the provision of a non-cash voucher` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10ZB(1) the provision is the provision of a benefit for the purposes of section 10ZA` MEANS
    IF `it is the provision of a non-cash voucher`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "references to the provision of a benefit include references to the provision of a non-cash voucher"

-- src:418 | (2) Where—
-- src:419 | (a) a non-cash voucher is received by any person from employment which is lower-paid employment as a minister of religion, and
-- src:420 | (b) the case would be one in which the conditions in section 10ZA(1)(a) to (d) above would be satisfied in relation to the provision of that voucher if that employment were not lower-paid employment as a minister of religion,
-- src:421 | sections 10 and 10ZA above shall have effect in relation to the provision of that voucher, and to any such payment in respect of the provision of that voucher as is mentioned in section 10ZA(2) above, as if that employment were not lower-paid employment as a minister of religion.
@ref s 10ZB(2) (src:418-421)
GIVEN `a non-cash voucher is received by the person from employment which is lower-paid employment as a minister of religion` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the case would satisfy the conditions in section 10ZA(1)(a) to (d) if that employment were not lower-paid employment as a minister of religion` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10ZB(2) sections 10 and 10ZA have effect as if the employment were not lower-paid employment as a minister of religion` MEANS
    IF     `a non-cash voucher is received by the person from employment which is lower-paid employment as a minister of religion`
       AND `the case would satisfy the conditions in section 10ZA(1)(a) to (d) if that employment were not lower-paid employment as a minister of religion`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where (a) ... and (b) ..." states the case; the subsection is silent otherwise

-- src:422 | (3) In this section “non-cash voucher” has the same meaning as in section 84 of ITEPA 2003.
@ref s 10ZB(3) (src:422-422)
GIVEN `it is a non-cash voucher within the meaning of section 84 of ITEPA 2003` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10ZB(3) the voucher is a non-cash voucher` MEANS
    IF `it is a non-cash voucher within the meaning of section 84 of ITEPA 2003`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“non-cash voucher” has the same meaning as in section 84 of ITEPA 2003"

§§ `s 10ZBA Liability of third party controller of sporting testimonial`

-- src:424 | (1) This section applies where—
-- src:425 | (a) a Class 1A contribution is payable for any tax year in respect of the whole or any part of general earnings received by an earner;
-- src:426 | (b) the general earnings, in so far as they are ones in respect of which such a contribution is payable, consist in a sporting testimonial payment; and
-- src:427 | (c) the controller of the sporting testimonial is not the person (“the relevant employer”) by whom, but for this section, the Class 1A contribution would be payable in accordance with section 10(2).
@ref s 10ZBA(1) (src:424-427)
GIVEN `a Class 1A contribution is payable for the tax year in respect of the whole or any part of general earnings received by the earner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the general earnings, so far as the contribution is payable on them, consist in a sporting testimonial payment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the controller of the sporting testimonial is not the relevant employer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10ZBA(1) section 10ZBA applies` MEANS
    IF     `a Class 1A contribution is payable for the tax year in respect of the whole or any part of general earnings received by the earner`
       AND `the general earnings, so far as the contribution is payable on them, consist in a sporting testimonial payment`
       AND `the controller of the sporting testimonial is not the relevant employer`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies where" the three conditions hold

-- src:428 | (2) The controller of the sporting testimonial, instead of the relevant employer, is liable to pay any Class 1A contribution in respect of the sporting testimonial payment.
@ref s 10ZBA(2) (src:428-428)
GIVEN `s 10ZBA(1) section 10ZBA applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10ZBA(2) the liability falls on the controller of the sporting testimonial` MEANS
    IF `s 10ZBA(1) section 10ZBA applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (2) is within "This section applies where" the conditions hold

-- src:429 | (3) Subsection (4) applies if—
-- src:430 | (a) the controller of the sporting testimonial pays an amount (“the amount to cover tax”) for the purpose of discharging any liability of the earner to income tax for any tax year (“the relevant year”), and
-- src:431 | (b) the income tax in question is tax chargeable in respect of the sporting testimonial payment or of the amount to cover tax.
-- src:432 | (4) For the purposes of this Act the amount to cover tax is to be treated as if it were general earnings consisting in the making of a sporting testimonial payment to the earner in the relevant year and falling, for the purposes of Class 1 contributions, to be left out of account in the computation of the earnings paid to or for the benefit of the earner.
@ref s 10ZBA(3), s 10ZBA(4) (src:429-432)
GIVEN `s 10ZBA(1) section 10ZBA applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the controller pays an amount for the purpose of discharging any liability of the earner to income tax for any tax year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the income tax is chargeable in respect of the sporting testimonial payment or of the amount to cover tax` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10ZBA(4) the amount to cover tax is treated as general earnings consisting in the making of a sporting testimonial payment to the earner` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`s 10ZBA(1) section 10ZBA applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (3) is in section 10ZBA, which "applies where" the conditions of subsection (1) hold
        IF `the controller pays an amount for the purpose of discharging any liability of the earner to income tax for any tax year` AND `the income tax is chargeable in respect of the sporting testimonial payment or of the amount to cover tax` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (4) applies if" (a) and (b) (marginal reading M1(a))

-- src:433 | (5) The controller of the sporting testimonial, instead of the relevant employer, is liable to pay any Class 1A contribution in respect of any further sporting testimonial payment treated as made to the earner in accordance with subsection (4).
@ref s 10ZBA(5) (src:433-433)
GIVEN `the payment is a further sporting testimonial payment treated as made to the earner in accordance with subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10ZBA(5) the liability for the further payment falls on the controller of the sporting testimonial` MEANS
    IF `the payment is a further sporting testimonial payment treated as made to the earner in accordance with subsection (4)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (5) speaks of "any further sporting testimonial payment treated as made ... in accordance with subsection (4)"

-- src:434 | (6) Expressions used in this section and section 226E of ITEPA 2003 (sporting testimonial payments) have the same meaning as in that section.
@ref s 10ZBA(6) (src:434-434)
GIVEN `the expression is used in this section and in section 226E of ITEPA 2003` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10ZBA(6) the expression has the meaning it has in section 226E of ITEPA 2003` MEANS
    IF `the expression is used in this section and in section 226E of ITEPA 2003`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Expressions used in this section and section 226E"

§§ `s 10ZC Class 1A contributions: power to make provision in consequence of retrospective tax legislation`

-- src:439 | (2) “Relevant retrospective tax provision” means a provision of the Income Tax Acts which—
-- src:440 | (a) has retrospective effect, and
-- src:441 | (b) affects the amount of general earnings received by an earner from an employment on which he is chargeable to income tax under the employment income Parts of ITEPA 2003 for a tax year.
@ref s 10ZC(2) (src:439-441)
GIVEN `the provision of the Income Tax Acts has retrospective effect` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it affects the amount of general earnings received by an earner from an employment on which he is chargeable to income tax under the employment income Parts of ITEPA 2003 for a tax year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10ZC(2) the provision is a relevant retrospective tax provision` MEANS
    IF     `the provision of the Income Tax Acts has retrospective effect`
       AND `it affects the amount of general earnings received by an earner from an employment on which he is chargeable to income tax under the employment income Parts of ITEPA 2003 for a tax year`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“Relevant retrospective tax provision” means a provision of the Income Tax Acts which (a) has retrospective effect, and (b) affects the amount of general earnings"

-- src:442 | (3) It does not matter whether the relevant retrospective tax provision was passed or made before the commencement day.
@ref s 10ZC(3) (src:442-442)
GIVEN `the relevant retrospective tax provision was passed or made before the commencement day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10ZC(3) the relevant retrospective tax provision counts` MEANS
    IF `the relevant retrospective tax provision was passed or made before the commencement day` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST TRUE    -- "It does not matter whether": both answers are "counts"

-- src:446 | (5) Regulations under this section may be made so as to have retrospective effect but must not have effect in relation to any time before 2nd December 2004.
@ref s 10ZC(5) (src:446-446)
GIVEN `the time to which the regulations would have effect` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10ZC(5) regulations under section 10ZC may have effect in relation to the time` MEANS
    IF `the time to which the regulations would have effect` LESS THAN (Date 2 12 2004)
    THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not have effect in relation to any time before 2nd December 2004"
    ELSE NOTHING       -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): from 2 December 2004 the text says "may be made so as to have retrospective effect" and no more; the grant is of RETROSPECTIVE effect and this function holds only the time, not the day the regulations are made, so a time inside the limit may or may not be retrospective; the flat negative speaks only of times before 2 December 2004

-- src:450 | (7) Regulations under this section—
-- src:451 | (a) may not impose any liability to pay a Class 1A contribution, and
-- src:452 | (b) may not increase the amount of any Class 1A contribution.
@ref s 10ZC(7) (src:450-452)
GIVEN `the regulations would impose a liability to pay a Class 1A contribution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the regulations would increase the amount of a Class 1A contribution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10ZC(7) regulations under section 10ZC may have that effect` MEANS
    IF `the regulations would impose a liability to pay a Class 1A contribution` OR `the regulations would increase the amount of a Class 1A contribution`
    THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Regulations under this section (a) may not impose any liability to pay a Class 1A contribution, and (b) may not increase the amount of any Class 1A contribution"
    ELSE NOTHING       -- NOTHING-kind (silent): regulations that neither impose nor increase are not addressed by subsection (7)

-- src:453 | (8) The powers conferred by this section are without prejudice to—
-- src:454 | (a) any liability to pay a Class 1A contribution which arises by virtue of any relevant retrospective tax provision, and
-- src:455 | (b) any powers conferred by or by virtue of any other provision of this Act or any other enactment.
@ref s 10ZC(8) (src:453-455)
GIVEN `the liability to pay a Class 1A contribution arises by virtue of a relevant retrospective tax provision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10ZC(8)(a) the powers are without prejudice to the liability` MEANS
    IF `the liability to pay a Class 1A contribution arises by virtue of a relevant retrospective tax provision`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (a) saves a liability "which arises by virtue of any relevant retrospective tax provision"

-- s 10ZC(10): the commencement day and "enactment" are defined as in s 4C(11); the text repeats the words, so the functions repeat the rule.
-- src:457 | (10) For the purposes of this section—
-- src:458 | “the commencement day” means the day on which the National Insurance Contributions Act 2006 was passed;
@ref s 10ZC(10) (src:457-458)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      `the day on which the National Insurance Contributions Act 2006 was passed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10ZC(10) the day is the commencement day` MEANS
    IF day EQUALS `the day on which the National Insurance Contributions Act 2006 was passed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“the commencement day” means the day on which the National Insurance Contributions Act 2006 was passed"

-- src:457 | (10) For the purposes of this section—
-- src:458 | “the commencement day” means the day on which the National Insurance Contributions Act 2006 was passed;
-- src:459 | “enactment” includes an instrument made under an Act.
@ref s 10ZC(10) (src:457-459)
GIVEN `it is an instrument made under an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10ZC(10) the thing is an enactment` MEANS
    IF `it is an instrument made under an Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“enactment” includes an instrument made under an Act"

§§ `s 10A Class 1B contributions`

-- src:462 | (1) Where for any tax year a person is accountable to the Inland Revenue in respect of income tax on general earnings of his employees in accordance with a PAYE settlement agreement, a Class 1B contribution shall be payable by him for that tax year in accordance with this section.
@ref s 10A(1) (src:462-462)
GIVEN `the person is accountable to the Inland Revenue in respect of income tax on general earnings of his employees in accordance with a PAYE settlement agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10A(1) a Class 1B contribution is payable by the person for the tax year` MEANS
    IF `the person is accountable to the Inland Revenue in respect of income tax on general earnings of his employees in accordance with a PAYE settlement agreement`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where for any tax year a person is accountable ... a Class 1B contribution shall be payable by him"

-- src:467 | (4) General earnings are chargeable emoluments for the purposes of subsection (2) above if, apart from section 6(2) or 10(6) above, the person accountable in accordance with the PAYE settlement agreement would be liable or entitled to pay secondary Class 1 contributions or Class 1A contributions in respect of them.
@ref s 10A(4) (src:467-467)
GIVEN `apart from section 6(2) or 10(6), the person accountable would be liable or entitled to pay secondary Class 1 contributions or Class 1A contributions in respect of the general earnings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10A(4) the general earnings are chargeable emoluments` MEANS
    IF `apart from section 6(2) or 10(6), the person accountable would be liable or entitled to pay secondary Class 1 contributions or Class 1A contributions in respect of the general earnings`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "General earnings are chargeable emoluments ... if, apart from section 6(2) or 10(6) above, the person accountable ... would be liable or entitled to pay secondary Class 1 contributions or Class 1A contributions in respect of them" (marginal reading M1(a))

-- src:468 | (5) Where—
-- src:469 | (a) the PAYE settlement agreement was entered into after the beginning of the tax year; and
-- src:470 | (b) Class 1 contributions were due in respect of any general earnings before it was entered into,
-- src:471 | those general earnings shall not be taken to be included in the PAYE settlement agreement.
@ref s 10A(5) (src:468-471)
GIVEN `the PAYE settlement agreement was entered into after the beginning of the tax year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Class 1 contributions were due in respect of the general earnings before it was entered into` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10A(5) the general earnings are taken to be included in the PAYE settlement agreement` MEANS
    IF `the PAYE settlement agreement was entered into after the beginning of the tax year` AND `Class 1 contributions were due in respect of the general earnings before it was entered into`
    THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "those general earnings shall not be taken to be included in the PAYE settlement agreement"
    ELSE NOTHING       -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where (a) ... and (b) ..." states the case; the subsection is silent otherwise

-- src:472 | (6) In subsection (3) above “the Class 1B percentage” means a percentage rate equal to the secondary percentage for the tax year in question.
@ref s 10A(6) (src:472-472)
GIVEN `s 9(2) the secondary percentage for the tax year in question` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 10A(6) the Class 1B percentage` MEANS `s 9(2) the secondary percentage for the tax year in question`

-- src:462 | (1) Where for any tax year a person is accountable to the Inland Revenue in respect of income tax on general earnings of his employees in accordance with a PAYE settlement agreement, a Class 1B contribution shall be payable by him for that tax year in accordance with this section.
-- src:463 | (2) The Class 1B contribution referred to in subsection (1) above is payable in respect of—
-- src:464 | (a) the amount of any of the general earnings included in the PAYE settlement agreement which are chargeable emoluments; and
-- src:465 | (b) the total amount of income tax in respect of which the person is accountable for the tax year in accordance with the PAYE settlement agreement.
-- src:466 | (3) The amount of the Class 1B contribution referred to in subsection (1) above shall be the Class 1B percentage of the aggregate of the amounts mentioned in paragraphs (a) and (b) of subsection (2) above.
@ref s 10A(2), s 10A(3) (src:462-466)
GIVEN `s 10A(1) a Class 1B contribution is payable by the person for the tax year` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the amount of the general earnings included in the PAYE settlement agreement which are chargeable emoluments` IS A NUMBER
      `the total amount of income tax in respect of which the person is accountable for the tax year in accordance with the PAYE settlement agreement` IS A NUMBER
      `s 10A(6) the Class 1B percentage` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 10A(3) the amount of the Class 1B contribution` MEANS
    IF `s 10A(1) a Class 1B contribution is payable by the person for the tax year` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (   `s 10A(6) the Class 1B percentage`
               TIMES (   `the amount of the general earnings included in the PAYE settlement agreement which are chargeable emoluments`
                      PLUS `the total amount of income tax in respect of which the person is accountable for the tax year in accordance with the PAYE settlement agreement`))
    ELSE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the amount is that of the contribution payable "referred to in subsection (1)"
